{#
    One entity's records, as a table.

    THE CELLS ARRIVE AS STRINGS. `ListController::rows()` has already turned every value into
    something printable, because `toValueObject()` does not answer scalars throughout — a
    `datetime` comes back as an array. Formatting here would move that trap into the template,
    where a wrong type is a runtime error on a page nobody tested with that field.

    `rows` IS KEYED BY PROPERTY, so the header and the body walk the same `columns` list and
    cannot drift apart. A column added to `ColumnBuilder` needs no change here.

    SORTING AND PAGING ARE PLAIN LINKS (002-003-0003). Turbo is already running — the layout's
    bare import starts it — and it intercepts same-origin links by itself, so a sort or a page
    change is a Turbo visit without a line of JavaScript here. The state travels in the URL,
    which is what makes any view of this list something that can be bookmarked or sent on.

    THE ADDRESSES ARE BUILT IN PHP, not here. `ListController` hands each column its `url` and
    its `ariaSort` ready-made, because assembling query strings in Twig means re-deciding in
    the template which parameters exist — and the controller is where they are read. The same
    holds for `row.editUrl` and `newUrl`, which story 002-006-0002 added.

    THE ACTION CELL CARRIES ITS OWN CLASS, and that is load-bearing. `admin-list__cell` is what
    `tools/harness-liste-pruefen.php` reads the table's values out of, in groups of one row's
    worth — wrapping a value in a link or adding a seventh cell of that class would make the
    gate read the wrong column. The action column is therefore `admin-list__action`, and its
    head cell carries no `aria-sort`, which the same gate uses to find the sorted column.

    THE FILTER BAR SITS OUTSIDE THE EMPTY CHECK (002-004-0002), and that is not a layout
    preference. Inside it, a filter that matches nothing would take its own controls off the page
    along with the table, and there would be no way left to undo it except editing the URL. For
    the same reason the empty state says *which* kind of empty it is: no records at all, or none
    that match the filter.

    IT IS A PLAIN GET FORM. The filter travels in the query string like the sort order does, so
    Turbo navigates the submit by itself and a filtered list stays a sendable address (ADR 0018
    §2). `page` is deliberately not among the hidden fields — `ListController::queryForm()`
    explains why.

    SEARCH AND FILTERS SHARE THAT ONE FORM (002-004-0003), so the browser always sends both and
    they narrow each other without either having to carry the other as a hidden field. The search
    box is `data-turbo-permanent` and the form `data-turbo-action="replace"`: the box survives the
    visit it triggers, with focus and caret, and typing does not fill the browser history. Both
    belong to `admin/list-search`, which is declared only on a page that actually has a box.

    THE SELECTION COLUMN HAS CLASSES OF ITS OWN (002-004-0004), for the reason the action cell
    does, and one more: `tools/harness-liste-pruefen.php` counts the rows by occurrences of
    `admin-list__row` and chunks the values by the number of sortable heads. A cell called
    `admin-list__cell` or a head called `admin-list__head` would therefore move every value one
    column over. The selection is `admin-list__select` and `admin-list__select-head`, and the
    head cell carries no `<a>`, which is what the head regex looks for.

    THE SELECTION IS A SECOND FORM AROUND THE TABLE. It is a POST and the query bar is a GET, and
    one form cannot contain another. The select-all box has no `name`, so it is never submitted —
    without JavaScript it simply does nothing, while the row boxes keep working and the bar stays
    visible with its initial text. `admin/list-select` hides the bar while nothing is ticked and
    counts what is.

    THE TWO ACTIONS ARE TWO SUBMIT BUTTONS OF THAT ONE FORM (002-004-0005), which is why the
    selection reaches both without being kept anywhere: the browser sends the ticked boxes along
    with whichever button was pressed, and `action` says which one it was. The change controls sit
    in a `<details>` — the collapse is the browser's own and costs no JavaScript — and the field
    is chosen by a radio button, so every type gets the control it deserves instead of one text
    box for all of them. Without JavaScript all of it works; what is missing is the confirmation
    before a delete, which `admin/list-select` adds.

    THE PROJECT'S RECORD ACTIONS ARE MORE SUBMIT BUTTONS OF THE SAME FORM (005-004-0004), for
    the reason the two above are: a second form inside this one is not allowed. A row button
    carries `selection.rowField` with its own record id, and the dispatcher then does not read
    `ids[]` at all — without that, pressing a button in row three would silently take every
    ticked row with it (ADR 0029 §4). A bulk button carries no id and gets the ticked ones. Both
    point at the same address through `formaction`; only the id tells them apart.

    THOSE BUTTONS CARRY `data-turbo="false"`, AND THAT IS NOT COSMETIC. Their main case is a file
    download, and a response Turbo fetched is a response the browser never offers to save — the
    click would do nothing at all, without an error. The attribute is part of the contract, which
    is why it is written here and stated in ADR 0029 §8 rather than left to be rediscovered.

    THE ROW BUTTON IS `admin-list__action-run` AND NOT `admin-list__row-action`, which looks
    like a worse name and is the safe one. `tools/harness-liste-pruefen.php` counts the rows by
    occurrences of the string `admin-list__row` and `tools/harness-projekt-seite-pruefen.php`
    does the same — any class beginning with it would be counted as a row, so three rows with
    two actions each would report as nine. The selection column one paragraph up carries the
    identical warning; this is the second time that substring has had to be avoided.

    AN `icon` BECOMES A HOOK, NOT A GLYPH. This package ships no icon set on purpose (`admin.css`
    says why), so it cannot draw one; it emits `data-icon` and a modifier class, and a project
    that wants a picture puts it there from its own stylesheet. The label is always written out,
    so the button stays readable with no icon and with an icon nobody styled.

    THE REPORT OF A FINISHED ACTION STANDS ABOVE THE BAR. `BulkController` redirects back here
    with the action, two counts and at most a few ids, and `ListController::report()` composes the
    sentence — the URL never carries prose.
#}{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block bodyAttributes %} class="admin"{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<main class="admin__main">
    <h1>{{ entityLabel }}</h1>

    <p class="admin-list__new"><a href="{{ newUrl }}">Neuer Datensatz</a></p>

{% if treeUrl %}
    <p class="admin-tree__switch"><a href="{{ treeUrl }}">Als Baum anzeigen</a></p>
{% endif %}

{% if report %}
    <p class="admin-list__report{% if not report.ok %} admin-list__report--problem{% endif %}" role="status">{{ report.text }}</p>
{% endif %}

{% if queryForm %}
    <form class="admin-list__filter" method="get" action="{{ queryForm.action }}"
          data-turbo-action="replace"{% if queryForm.search is not null %} data-controller="admin-list-search"{% endif %}>
{% for name, value in queryForm.hidden %}
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ name }}" value="{{ value }}">
{% endfor %}
{% if queryForm.search is not null %}
        <p class="admin-list__filter-field">
            <label for="list-search">Suche</label>
            <input type="search" id="list-search" name="q" value="{{ queryForm.search }}"
                   autocomplete="off" data-turbo-permanent
                   data-admin-list-search-target="box">
        </p>
{% endif %}
{% for field in queryForm.fields %}
        <p class="admin-list__filter-field">
            <label for="filter-{{ field.property }}">{{ field.label }}</label>
{% if field.type == 'integer' %}
            <input type="number" id="filter-{{ field.property }}" name="filter[{{ field.property }}]" value="{{ field.value }}" step="1">
{% elseif field.type == 'boolean' %}
            <select id="filter-{{ field.property }}" name="filter[{{ field.property }}]">
                <option value="">Alle</option>
                <option value="true"{{ field.value == 'true' ? ' selected' : '' }}>Ja</option>
                <option value="false"{{ field.value == 'false' ? ' selected' : '' }}>Nein</option>
            </select>
{% else %}
            <select id="filter-{{ field.property }}" name="filter[{{ field.property }}]">
                <option value="">Alle</option>
                <option value="{{ queryForm.unsetValue }}"{{ field.value == queryForm.unsetValue ? ' selected' : '' }}>Nicht gesetzt</option>
{% for option in field.options %}
                <option value="{{ option.value }}"{{ field.value == option.value ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ option.label }}</option>
{% endfor %}
            </select>
{% if field.truncated %}
            <span class="admin-list__filter-hint">Nur die ersten {{ field.options|length }} Einträge zur Auswahl</span>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
        </p>
{% endfor %}
        <p class="admin-list__filter-actions">
            <button type="submit">Anwenden</button>
{% if queryForm.resetUrl %}
            <a class="admin-list__filter-reset" href="{{ queryForm.resetUrl }}">Zurücksetzen</a>
{% endif %}
        </p>
    </form>
{% endif %}

{% if rows is empty %}
{% if queryForm and queryForm.active %}
    <p class="admin__hint">Kein Datensatz passt zu dieser Einschränkung.</p>
{% else %}
    <p class="admin__hint">Für diese Entität gibt es noch keine Datensätze.</p>
{% endif %}
{% else %}
{% if selection %}
    <form class="admin-list__bulk" method="post" action="{{ selection.action }}"
          data-controller="admin-list-select">
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ selection.tokenField }}" value="{{ selection.token }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="query" value="{{ selection.query }}">
{% endif %}
    <table class="admin-list">
        <thead>
            <tr>
{% if selection %}
                <th scope="col" class="admin-list__select-head">
                    <input type="checkbox" aria-label="Alle Zeilen dieser Seite markieren"
                           data-admin-list-select-target="all">
                </th>
{% endif %}
{% for column in columns %}
                <th scope="col" class="admin-list__head" aria-sort="{{ column.ariaSort }}">
                    <a class="admin-list__sort admin-list__sort--{{ column.ariaSort }}" href="{{ column.url }}">{{ column.label }}</a>
                </th>
{% endfor %}
                <th scope="col" class="admin-list__action-head"></th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
{% for row in rows %}
            <tr class="admin-list__row">
{% if selection %}
                <td class="admin-list__select">
{% if row.id %}
                    <input type="checkbox" name="ids[]" value="{{ row.id }}"
                           aria-label="Datensatz {{ row.id }} markieren"
                           data-admin-list-select-target="row">
{% endif %}
                </td>
{% endif %}
{% for column in columns %}
                <td class="admin-list__cell">{{ row.cells[column.property] }}</td>
{% endfor %}
                <td class="admin-list__action">
{% if row.editUrl %}
                    <a href="{{ row.editUrl }}">Bearbeiten</a>
{% endif %}
{% if selection and row.id %}
{% for action in rowActions %}
                    <button type="submit" class="admin-list__action-run{% if action.icon %} admin-list__action-run--icon{% endif %}"
                            name="{{ selection.rowField }}" value="{{ row.id }}"
                            formaction="{{ action.url }}" formmethod="post" data-turbo="false"
                            {% if action.icon %}data-icon="{{ action.icon }}" {% endif %}>{{ action.label }}</button>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
                </td>
            </tr>
{% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
{% if selection %}
        <div class="admin-list__bulk-bar" data-admin-list-select-target="bar">
            <span class="admin-list__bulk-count" aria-live="polite"
                  data-admin-list-select-target="count">Keine Zeile markiert</span>
            <button type="submit" class="admin-list__bulk-delete"
                    name="{{ selection.actionField }}" value="{{ selection.delete }}">Löschen</button>
{% for action in rowActions %}{% if action.bulk %}
            <button type="submit" class="admin-list__bulk-action{% if action.icon %} admin-list__bulk-action--icon{% endif %}"
                    formaction="{{ action.url }}" formmethod="post" data-turbo="false"
                    {% if action.icon %}data-icon="{{ action.icon }}" {% endif %}>{{ action.label }}</button>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% if selection.fields is not empty %}
            <details class="admin-list__bulk-change">
                <summary>Ein Feld ändern</summary>
{% for field in selection.fields %}
                <p class="admin-list__bulk-field">
                    <label for="bulk-{{ field.property }}">
                        <input type="radio" name="field" value="{{ field.property }}"> {{ field.label }}
                    </label>
{% if field.type == 'boolean' %}
                    <select id="bulk-{{ field.property }}" name="value[{{ field.property }}]">
                        <option value="true">Ja</option>
                        <option value="false">Nein</option>
                    </select>
{% elseif field.type == 'select' %}
                    <select id="bulk-{{ field.property }}" name="value[{{ field.property }}]">
{% for option in field.options %}
                        <option value="{{ option.value }}">{{ option.label }}</option>
{% endfor %}
                    </select>
{% elseif field.type == 'integer' %}
                    <input type="number" step="1" id="bulk-{{ field.property }}" name="value[{{ field.property }}]">
{% elseif field.type == 'decimal' or field.type == 'float' %}
                    <input type="number" step="any" id="bulk-{{ field.property }}" name="value[{{ field.property }}]">
{% else %}
                    <input type="text" id="bulk-{{ field.property }}" name="value[{{ field.property }}]"{% if field.maxlength %} maxlength="{{ field.maxlength }}"{% endif %}>
{% endif %}
                </p>
{% endfor %}
                <p class="admin-list__bulk-apply">
                    <button type="submit" name="{{ selection.actionField }}"
                            value="{{ selection.change }}">Auf die Markierten anwenden</button>
                </p>
            </details>
{% endif %}
        </div>
    </form>
{% endif %}

    <nav class="admin-pager" aria-label="Seitennavigation">
{% if pagination.prevUrl %}
        <a class="admin-pager__step" href="{{ pagination.prevUrl }}" rel="prev">Zurück</a>
{% else %}
        <span class="admin-pager__step admin-pager__step--off" aria-disabled="true">Zurück</span>
{% endif %}
        <span class="admin-pager__state">Seite {{ pagination.page }} von {{ pagination.pages }} · {{ pagination.total }} Datensätze</span>
{% if pagination.nextUrl %}
        <a class="admin-pager__step" href="{{ pagination.nextUrl }}" rel="next">Weiter</a>
{% else %}
        <span class="admin-pager__step admin-pager__step--off" aria-disabled="true">Weiter</span>
{% endif %}
    </nav>
{% endif %}
</main>
{% endblock %}
